From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Shape Healing - only update lwire when the loop iteration is not
 skipped in connectWiresToWiresImpl

**Backports [Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1331](https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/pull/1331)** (open,
third-party author, pinned to commit `7557161a3dbe7e1ba18a3e63e1e104830d8c24c5`), fixing
[OCCT#1330](https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/issues/1330). Audited and queued in
[#323](https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/issues/323).

`ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds::connectWiresToWiresImpl` (the same static helper patch `0004` already
touches for a different bug, #310) has a "find the next unconsumed wire" loop:

```cpp
for (i = 1; i <= arrwires->Length(); i++)
{
  if (!aSel.ContWire(i))
  {
    lwire = i;
    sewd->Add(TopoDS::Wire(arrwires->Value(lwire)));
    aSel.LoadList(lwire);

    if (sewd->NbEdges() > 0)
    {
      break;
    }
    sewd->Clear();
  }
}
```

It sets `lwire = i` **before** checking whether the wire it just loaded (`sewd`) actually has any
edges. If `sewd->NbEdges() == 0` (the wire is skipped, `sewd->Clear()`'d, and the loop continues to
the next `i`), `lwire` is left pointing at the skipped wire's index instead of being reset. If every
remaining candidate is likewise skipped, the loop finishes with `lwire` still holding a stale index
from a wire that was never actually added to the result — the caller's `if (lwire == -1) { done =
true; }` check never fires (since `lwire` isn't `-1`, it's a stale positive index), so `done` stays
false and the outer `while (!done)` loop's next iteration reads `sewd->Edge(1)` on data that no
longer corresponds to what `lwire` claims — invalid-memory access.

**Fix:** only assign `lwire = i` once the wire has actually been accepted (`sewd->NbEdges() > 0`),
matching the exact reordering upstream ships — the `sewd->Add`/`aSel.LoadList` calls move up to use
the loop variable `i` directly (since `lwire` no longer holds a valid value at that point), and
`lwire = i` moves inside the `if (sewd->NbEdges() > 0)` block, right before the `break`.

**Validation** (fast path, no full rebuild — see the `#0001` entry above for the override-link
technique): translated the upstream TCL test (`tests/bugs/heal/bug1330`) to C++ — a valid closed
triangle wire plus a single **internal-orientation** edge (its own one-edge "wire"), fed to
`ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds::ConnectEdgesToWires`. SIGSEGVs (`ShapeExtend_WireData::Edge` reading
invalid data, via `connectWiresToWiresImpl` → `ConnectWiresToWires` → `ConnectEdgesToWires`) 100% of
the time on stock p1 + patches 0001–0006; returns a valid 1-wire result after this patch.

Reported upstream as [OCCT#1330](https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/issues/1330) /
[OCCT#1331](https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/pull/1331) (third party, open — pin to the SHA
above and re-verify if it changes in review).

**Retire** once the bundled OCCT includes this fix.
---
 src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds.cxx | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds.cxx
index e6f5c7d3..a1b2c3d4 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeAnalysis/ShapeAnalysis_FreeBounds.cxx
@@ -403,12 +403,12 @@ static void connectWiresToWiresImpl(
       {
         if (!aSel.ContWire(i))
         {
-          lwire = i;
-          sewd->Add(TopoDS::Wire(arrwires->Value(lwire)));
-          aSel.LoadList(lwire);
+          sewd->Add(TopoDS::Wire(arrwires->Value(i)));
+          aSel.LoadList(i);

           if (sewd->NbEdges() > 0)
           {
+            lwire = i;
             break;
           }
           sewd->Clear();
